<title>UK: Phillips says reopens 100,000 bpd UK Tees refinery.</title>
<headline>Phillips says reopens 100,000 bpd UK Tees refinery.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phillips Petroleum Co has reopened its 100,000 barrels-per-day refinery on north Tees after it was shut for inspection last week following a small fire, a company spokeswoman said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The refinery, which was shut for inspection after a small fire on Thursday, restarted on Sunday, company spokeman Paula Hopson said.</p>
<p>The refinery, situated in northeast England, is jointly owned by Phillips and Imperial Chemical Industries Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714.</p>
